  "description": "CR 611.2a whole card: the animation outlives Titania's Song and ends at cleanup",
  "note": "Bonesplitter makes all three of the Song's parts observable at once: a noncreature artifact (so the layer-4 animation reaches it), mana value 1 (so the 1/1 survives), and an Equip keyword read off the post-layer keyword map (so the layer-6 strip shows). Angelic Edict exiles the Song, which is leaving the battlefield, and the Bonesplitter stays a 1/1 with no Equip for the rest of the turn. Jade Statue, cast after the Song left, is CR 611.2c's probe: the affected set was fixed when the effect began, so the Statue is not animated and keeps its own ability, which it activates in combat. The animation ends in the cleanup step: on bob's turn the Bonesplitter is a bare artifact with its Equip back.",
